# qmldir — explicit module manifest for quickshell/modules/appearance/
# (quick task 260828-ah9). Mirrors every sibling module manifest's own
# standing instruction (see modules/packages/qmldir, modules/security/qmldir,
# modules/osd/qmldir): any .qml type added to this directory that is NOT
# declared below becomes unresolvable, with no load error — it simply
# reads `undefined` forever. qml-import-check enforces this. Any FUTURE
# type added here MUST be declared in the SAME COMMIT that creates it.
#
# ── THE `singleton` KEYWORD IS LOAD-BEARING ───────────────────────────
# AppearanceBackend carries `pragma Singleton` AND is marked `singleton`
# below — both required, per modules/packages/qmldir's own binary-verified
# finding: without the qmldir keyword, a bare `AppearanceBackend.iconThemes`
# -style access resolves to `undefined` forever and the object is never
# constructed. Removing either one is a silent, error-free failure.
#
# AppearanceBackend is the singleton that owns icon-theme and font state.
# Settings > Appearance's two SelectRows, the Atelier's Icons/Fonts/
# Catalogue tabs, the launcher's `icon`/`font` routes and the bar's clock
# drawer are readers of ONE backend, never four backends.
module qs.modules.appearance

singleton AppearanceBackend 1.0 AppearanceBackend.qml

# ── Surfaces (Task 2) ──
# The Atelier: its own FloatingWindow behind a LazyLoader, the Workbench
# pattern. NOT a singleton — shell.qml mounts one instance, the same
# posture Bar/Dashboard/Workbench have in the parent modules/qmldir.
Atelier 1.0 Atelier.qml

# The Atelier's tab strip and its Icons/Fonts panes, split the way
# Workbench splits its own three panes rather than one long file.
AtTabBar 1.0 AtTabBar.qml
AtIconsTab 1.0 AtIconsTab.qml
AtFontsTab 1.0 AtFontsTab.qml

# AtCatalogueTab (Task 3, D-04) — the third pane, browse + install.
AtCatalogueTab 1.0 AtCatalogueTab.qml

# Operator round 1 (2c/2e) — the shared resizable-rail grip, reused by
# AtIconsTab/AtFontsTab/AtCatalogueTab rather than three divergent copies.
AtRailGrip 1.0 AtRailGrip.qml

# Operator round 1, defect 1 — the shared uninstall-confirmation overlay,
# mounted once in Atelier.qml and driven off AppearanceBackend.uninstallPlan.
AtUninstallConfirm 1.0 AtUninstallConfirm.qml
